<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramnagar Ramlila</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">19th century–present</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ramnagar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramlila">Ramlila</a> is a month-long performance of the Ramlila held each year at Ramnagar, across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varanasi">Varanasi</a>, under the patronage of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharajas</a> of Benares. Begun in the 19th century, it is staged in different parts of the town, which serve as fixed sets, and the audience moves with the action. It is regarded as the most traditional of all Ramlila performances.</p></div>
